&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a Designer to join Abnormal AI&#39;s Creative Services team. As a member of the in-house studio, you&#39;ll play a key role in bringing our visual identity to life across a wide range of touchpoints, including campaigns and digital surfaces to social, events, and brand content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on execution role for a designer who is comfortable working across a broad spectrum of asset types and moving fluidly between projects. You care deeply about craft and quality, you&#39;re comfortable taking direction and running with it, and you thrive in a fast-moving, collaborative environment. You bring a genuine curiosity for how AI tools can accelerate and elevate your creative process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce high-quality design assets across brand touchpoints, including web, campaigns, social, events, and print.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute creative across a variety of formats and asset types, working from briefs, established design systems, and creative direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with marketing, content, and web partners to deliver cohesive, on-brand creative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to web-forward creative execution across digital surfaces and campaigns, demonstrating fluency in how design systems translate to the web.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively integrate AI tools into your creative workflow, using them to accelerate production, explore options, and push the work further.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain brand consistency across all deliverables, ensuring work aligns with Abnormal AI&#39;s visual identity standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple projects simultaneously, prioritizing effectively and communicating proactively on timelines and capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
