&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enterprise Platform Engineer helps build and run secure, reliable, and increasingly AI-enabled workforce technology across identity, endpoints, SaaS, collaboration, network, and office IT. You will turn policies, runbooks, telemetry, and employee needs into practical automations and self-service experiences that reduce manual work and improve the employee experience. You will work closely with experienced engineers and cross-functional partners while building ownership of defined platform capabilities and connected systems. You will use AI tools as part of your day-to-day engineering workflow and develop an AI-forward mindset grounded in security, observability, thoughtful evaluation, and human judgment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reflects Abnormal&#39;s VOICE values. You move with velocity, design for long-term ownership and governance, use data with intellectual honesty, stay close to customer needs, and aim for excellence in reliability and simplicity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and support automations for joiner, mover, and leaver flows, access requests, device management, deprovisioning, and common employee IT needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support identity and access capabilities using SSO, MFA, least privilege, birthright access, directory and group models, standards-based provisioning, and device trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help operate zero-touch device provisioning and management for macOS and Windows, including application packaging, patch automation, policy compliance, and drift detection.&lt;/li&gt;
