&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Outbound Product Management is R&amp;amp;D&#39;s operating layer in the field — the function that sits between what we build and how it actually performs with customers. As an Outbound Product Manager focused on Identity, you&#39;ll start by owning the field motion for our Identity Threat Protection launch: running structured field validation before a playbook exists, testing messaging in live conversations, and diagnosing whether early friction reflects a real product gap or a positioning gap. As the product matures to GA, you&#39;ll transition into standing ownership of the identity product area — generating ongoing signal, running adoption diagnostics, and supporting high-touch customer situations that require real identity depth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a feedback-intake role. You won&#39;t just relay what you hear in customer conversations — you&#39;ll apply judgment to it. That means distinguishing a real product gap from a positioning gap or a sales-motion gap, validating that a pattern holds across accounts rather than resting on a single anecdote, and knowing when a read is solid enough to bring back to PM versus when it needs more digging.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your identity background is what makes this role work: you&#39;ll be the person in the room who can go toe-to-toe with a customer&#39;s security team on IAM, authentication, and access patterns, and translate what you hear into something Product and Product Marketing can act on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Near-term (Identity Threat Protection launch):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the EA-to-GA motion for the Identity Threat Protection launch: demos, deep dives, and POVs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test messaging hypotheses in live deals alongside Sales Engineers, and diagnose competitive loss reasons — product gap vs. framing gap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brief PM with pattern analysis across accounts, and document what works to produce a proven playbook ready for SE enablement at GA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ongoing (as the product area matures):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transition into standing ownership of the identity product area, carrying it forward permanently as the product moves through its lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run adoption diagnostics on identity features, and support technical evaluations in competitive renewals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide consultative escalation support on complex identity-related customer situations, growing into direct participation on the most complex cases over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Marketing as a standing collaborator on identity messaging and competitive positioning as new pressures emerge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-Have Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years as a Sales Engineer, Solutions Engineer, or similarly technical customer-facing role at an identity security company (IAM, IGA, PAM, SSO/authentication, or adjacent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of identity security concepts: authentication flows, access patterns, privilege escalation, account takeover dynamics, and how identity threats actually show up in customer environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has worked in a pre-launch or early-stage product environment before a playbook existed — can point to a specific program, motion, or deliverable they built from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication — able to turn technical identity conversations into a defensible, pattern-based narrative for both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credible in front of technical buyers and security teams; equally comfortable in a live customer deep-dive and an internal roadmap review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has operated in a field intelligence or outbound-facing capacity — SE, OPM, Field PM, or equivalent — where the primary output is pattern synthesis and product insight, not quota attainment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has taken a field observation from raw signal to a documented recommendation that a PM or GTM team acted on, not just surfacing issues, but following through with evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with account takeover (ATO), session/privilege abuse, or identity-based attack patterns specifically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior involvement in a new-product launch, early-access program, or beta motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running or presenting in structured cross-functional forums (POV reviews, launch/GTM syncs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using AI tools to synthesize patterns across large sets of qualitative input (support tickets, call transcripts, win/loss notes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role Matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identity is one of the fastest-growing and highest-stakes areas of our product line, and the difference between a real identity insight and a surface-level one shows up immediately in front of a customer&#39;s security team. This role exists to bring genuine identity depth into the field motion from day one — starting with a brand-new launch, and growing into permanent ownership of the area as it matures. You’ll be trusted to run engagements independently and build real domain credibility, with a clear path to owning the highest-stakes identity situations as you grow into the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
