&lt;h1&gt;About the Role&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is looking for a Salesforce Administrator to work our day-to-day Salesforce administrative ticket queue and backlog. You&#39;ll take ownership of tickets in the queue — scoping the work, shipping fast declarative fixes, and clearing backlog — while supporting cross-functional teams like Marketing Operations along the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an administration-focused role. You&#39;ll work within Salesforce&#39;s declarative tools — Flow, validation rules, page layouts, permission sets — rather than writing code, and you&#39;ll partner closely with our broader systems and Marketing Operations teams to prioritize backlog and escalate anything that needs deeper platform or security expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work the Salesforce administrative ticket queue and backlog end to end: scope complexity, prioritize, and ship resolutions for Sales Ops and cross-functional GTM stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the dedicated Salesforce point of contact for top of funnel workstreams, supporting needs like campaign infrastructure and lead/contact routing and personalization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain declarative solutions using clicks-not-code: Flow, validation rules, page layouts, record types, permission sets, and reports/dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide fast, accurate day-to-day Salesforce support to end users across the GTM org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use and evolve AI-assisted tooling to speed up requirements gathering and solution design, and to keep documentation and end-user guides current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate requests that require custom development, platform security changes, or integration work to the appropriate specialist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and report on backlog health — ticket volume, aging, and throughput — flagging capacity risk before it becomes a bottleneck.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;AI Forward Hiring&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is expected to use AI as a core part of how the work gets done, not just to be aware of it. You&#39;ll actively use and extend AI-assisted tooling to speed up requirements documentation and solution design — treating it as a lever to clear more backlog, not a novelty. Strong candidates can point to concrete examples of using AI tools to move faster and produce more thorough, reliable work, not just experimenting with them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Must Have Skills&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–4 years of hands-on Salesforce Administration experience in a production, multi-user org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce Administrator certification required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong declarative configuration skills: Flow, validation rules, permission sets, page layouts, record types, and reports/dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work a high-volume ticket queue: prioritization, resolution, and clear communication with non-technical requesters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Sales and/or Marketing Operations stakeholders in Salesforce (campaign infrastructure, routing, lead/contact management)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to scope and estimate work and communicate realistic timelines to requesters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Nice to Have Skills&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Salesforce CPQ from an end-user or configuration perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI-assisted development or documentation tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or using internal automation/AI tooling to speed up support workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
