&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI’s Sales Operations team is the connective tissue between our go-to-market motion and the data, systems, and processes that power it. As an Analyst on the Sales Operations (“SOPs”) team, you&#39;ll be the first point of contact for our revenue-facing employees—onboarding new hires into our tech stack and operating cadences, owning key reporting initiatives, and spotting the manual, repeatable work worth automating. This is a high-visibility, high-impact role for someone energized by variety, who loves solving problems end-to-end, and who wants to build a career in revenue operations at a category-leading cybersecurity company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New Hire Onboarding&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the SOPS point of contact for all incoming new hires during their first 30 days. Proactively driving formalized sessions on their onboarding journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct AE walkthroughs of their territory, operating cadences, addressing questions on systems/tools, and going into depth on what it takes to be a successful AE at Abnormal AE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assign territory and accounts to new hires - validation of accounts in territory, confirming holdovers, and executing account moves in partnership with with Regional Directors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve the reporting framework to properly assess overall AE performance for reps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the enablement team and Sales Leaders to create action plans and surface findings of any AE performance gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and continuously improve the SOPS onboarding checklist and documents. Ensuring resources for AEs remain up to date and are effective resources to answer common questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the creation, distribution, and analysis of key Field Operations initiatives such as:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New hire ramp &amp;amp; tenured AE reporting: activity metrics, tool adoption, quota attainment progression. Uncovering what’s working and what the risks are.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SPIFF tracking and payout eligibility reports (weekly / end-of-quarter)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the business running operationally by being responsible for data hygiene scorecards: missing next steps, stale close dates, incomplete fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad-hoc reporting requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Territory Operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate territory assignments following re-carves or headcount changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support quarterly and annual planning cycles with data pulls and cleanup sprints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Monthly hygiene clean up activities in SFDC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute ongoing Salesforce hygiene projects: account merges, ownership transfers, field standardization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sales Operations Automation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the shift from manual ticket logging to automated resolution for common issues—driving smoother field execution and cleaner processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring SFDC errors (Opportunities, Accounts, CPQ) and route patterns to Sales Systems/IT for automated fixes, not one-off tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with IT and Sales Systems to build and ship automation for repeat manual processes and systems errors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own triage and response for inbound AErequests, using volume patterns to prioritize what gets automated next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must Haves&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-3 years of experience in sales operations, revenue operations, business operations, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on Salesforce experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and a process-first mindset — you catch the thing everyone else misses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, professional written communication; comfortable in a Slack-heavy async environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple requests simultaneously and prioritize under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Excel / Google Sheets for data validation and light analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses AI tools as a daily part of the workflow to move faster and deliver higher-quality work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SFDC, Outreach, Gong, Highspot, or comparable GTM tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Sigma, Gong, or other BI/reporting platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a help-queue or ticketing environment (Zendesk, Jira, Slack-based triage)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to territory management, quota setting, or SPIFF program administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in B2B SaaS or cybersecurity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To support collaboration with the team and stakeholders, candidates located in Eastern Time Zone is strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
