&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Marketing Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to help shape the next chapter of our core email security business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly strategic PMM role at the intersection of Product, customers, and go-to-market. Abnormal is innovating at an incredible pace, and we’re looking for someone who can step back from a fast-moving roadmap, connect the dots across products and capabilities, and turn technical innovation into clear, differentiated stories that resonate with customers and drive the business forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work closely with Product and R&amp;amp;D to bring customer, market, and competitive insight into product and commercialization decisions, then own how those decisions come to life through positioning, launches, sales plays, and enablement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior member of the team, you’ll also be a strategic partner and mentor to other product marketers, helping raise the bar for PMM craft across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who thrives in ambiguity, moves quickly, and is comfortable rolling up their sleeves to get a launch out the door.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create compelling, differentiated messaging and positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring product lines to market via internal and external launches, including sales enablement, press, digital, and other channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across marketing teams to drive demand and pipeline for our product lines with acquisition and upsell messaging for multi-phase buyer journey.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support incremental updates and feature launches throughout the year with end-to-end launch strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and keep fresh content including collateral, thought leadership and solution presentations, website content, videos, blogs and more to execute communication strategies and accelerate the buyer’s journey.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct customer research to understand needs and requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable our sales teams and channel partners on the joint solution and the value proposition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a speaker externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must Haves&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years of experience at a B2B SaaS cybersecurity company, with 3+ years in product marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Written samples of external-facing content for cybersecurity buyers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running product launches in a high velocity environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical curiosity with past examples of explaining complex technical concepts to buyers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker who is able to get to work quickly and execute independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to effectively influence both internal and external stakeholders across all levels of the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep curiosity, excellent listening and empathy skills, and ability to get things done in a collaborative team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for Abnormal&#39;s mission and the success of our customers, partners, and community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoys public speaking and evangelizing cybersecurity topics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with defining GTM strategies at growth-phase cybersecurity companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
