&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is looking for a Senior Revenue Accountant to join our Accounting team, reporting to Crystal He. In this role, you will own key areas of the revenue close process, preparing and reviewing audit-ready reconciliations, workpapers, journal entries, and analyses that support monthly close, financial reporting, and external audit requirements. This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced accountant to gain meaningful ownership and exposure to technical revenue accounting in a high-growth SaaS environment, while partnering closely with experienced revenue and technical accounting professionals. The ideal candidate operates independently, exercises strong judgment, and is motivated to strengthen how revenue accounting operates by standardizing processes, enhancing controls, and leveraging automation and AI-enabled workflows to improve efficiency, accuracy, and scalability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the preparation and review of monthly revenue-related reconciliations, rollforwards, and supporting schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review journal entries and flux analyses for revenue, deferred revenue, accounts receivable, commissions, and other related accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain complete, audit-ready documentation for recurring close activities, including organized workpapers, reconciliations, and supporting evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead assigned revenue close deliverables, ensuring work is completed accurately, timely, and in accordance with established policies and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve accounting issues, unusual items, and reconciling differences in partnership with cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support external audits by preparing support, coordinating requests, responding to inquiries, and documenting accounting positions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Deal Desk, FP&amp;amp;A, Legal, and other teams to resolve operational issues and improve upstream process quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and drive opportunities to streamline close activities through standardization, automation, and AI-enabled workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of progressive accounting, audit, or related finance experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of U.S. GAAP, with experience applying revenue recognition guidance and related accounting principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning or leading recurring close activities, reconciliations, and financial analyses in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with excellent attention to detail, and the ability to identify issues, evaluate root causes, and implement solutions with limited oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel skills, including reconciliations, lookups, and analysis of large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying ASC 606 and ASC 340-40 in a SaaS revenue accounting environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a Big Four public accounting firm, a high-growth pre-IPO company, or a publicly traded technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP, billing, and close-management systems such as NetSuite, Salesforce, Maxio, or FloQast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA license (or active progress toward CPA) and interest in leveraging AI and automation to improve accounting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
