&lt;h1&gt;About the Role&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is looking for a Salesforce Administrator to own our Salesforce CPQ platform and manage the requirements intake process for incoming Salesforce requests. You&#39;ll be the front door for new requests: gathering requirements, scoping complexity, and routing work to the right owner, while also owning CPQ configuration and quote-to-cash workflows end to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role blends two things: deep ownership of CPQ, and ownership of the intake process itself. You&#39;re the person who takes a request from a raw ask to a scoped, actionable ticket, and you&#39;re also the specialist who configures and maintains the pricing and quoting engine our sales team runs on every deal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end Salesforce CPQ configuration: product rules, price rules, bundles, and approval flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage quote-to-cash workflows, including contract generation and e-signature integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for CPQ end users, providing troubleshooting, enablement, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the requirements intake process for incoming Salesforce administrative requests: gather requirements, scope complexity, and route or prioritize work appropriately.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle intake and resolution of low-complexity Salesforce configuration requests directly, keeping quick wins from adding to the broader backlog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use and evolve AI-assisted tooling to speed up requirements gathering, documentation, and solution scoping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Sales Operations, Marketing Operations, and other Salesforce administrators to keep requests moving smoothly from ask to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;AI Forward Hiring&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is expected to use AI as a core part of how the work gets done, not just to be aware of it. You&#39;ll actively use and extend AI-assisted tooling to speed up requirements gathering, documentation, and solution scoping — treating it as a lever to move requests faster, not a novelty. Strong candidates can point to concrete examples of using AI tools to move faster and produce more thorough, reliable work, not just experimenting with them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Must Have Skills&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of hands-on Salesforce Administration experience, including CPQ configuration in a production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce Administrator certification required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on Salesforce CPQ configuration experience: product rules, price rules, bundles, and approval flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with quote-to-cash workflows and contract/e-signature tools (e.g., DocuSign, SpotDraft)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong requirements-gathering and scoping skills — able to translate ambiguous requests into clear, actionable tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort owning a process end-to-end, from initial intake conversation through routing and prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Nice to Have Skills&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce CPQ Specialist certification or experience implementing CPQ Systems (Nue.io, Conga, Dealhub, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broader Salesforce declarative configuration experience (Flow, validation rules, permission sets) beyond CPQ&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Sales, Marketing Operations, or RevOps stakeholders directly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI-assisted requirements-gathering or documentation tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
