&lt;h1&gt;Senior Software Engineer - Identity Security Posture Management (ISPM)&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With identity now serving as the main attack vector for modern enterprises, having complete visibility to &lt;strong&gt;understand every identity in your environment and proactively eliminate risk before it&#39;s exploited&lt;/strong&gt; is more essential than ever. As one of Abnormal&#39;s fastest-growing divisions, ISPM is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to drive the technical roadmap and guide an engineering team in developing the next generation of identity security defenses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on technical leadership role at the intersection of &lt;strong&gt;identity security&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;distributed systems engineering&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;ll write code, design systems, set technical standards, and mentor engineers — while partnering closely with Product Management to define what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own the full stack: backend services that continuously evaluate millions of identity configurations, a frontend used daily by enterprise security teams, and the data infrastructure that powers posture scoring and proactive risk remediation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Technical Strategy &amp;amp; Leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the ISPM technical roadmap by converting product requirements into robust system designs, mapping out implementation phases, and making strategic build-vs-extend decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, design, and scale core identity security posture systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate and drive cross-functional technical alliances with platform teams across the security and identity stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author, review, and evaluate technical design documents while facilitating architectural discussions and design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish, promote, and uphold engineering best practices across the sub-team, focusing on testing, code quality, API design, and observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Software Engineering &amp;amp; Architecture&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Construct and scale high-performance backend services using &lt;strong&gt;Go&lt;/strong&gt; — including event-driven systems, REST/gRPC APIs, cron jobs, and integration layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain user-facing interfaces using &lt;strong&gt;React/TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt; — focusing on policy dashboards, identity visualization, and mitigation workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, model, and optimize database schemas capable of handling large-scale multi-tenant identity workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement event-driven architectures using &lt;strong&gt;Kafka&lt;/strong&gt; as a message queue to manage asynchronous workflows and ensure continuous evaluation of identity postures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain operational reliability and service health through standard runbooks, feature flags, and robust monitoring setups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Team Collaboration &amp;amp; Delivery&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support, mentor, and guide a distributed team of 3-4 engineers located across India and Singapore.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Product Managers and EM to align on technical strategy, prioritize roadmaps, and deliver quarterly key results and milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own operational health for all services — on-call rotation, incident response, and SLO management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the team representative during organizational alignment, review sessions, and client interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Have Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of software development experience, including at least &lt;strong&gt;2+ years&lt;/strong&gt; in a tech lead or senior technical leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of &lt;strong&gt;mentoring engineers&lt;/strong&gt; and elevating the overall technical standards of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional system architecture skills—experienced in designing and running scalable, multi-tenant, event-driven distributed systems at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience with &lt;strong&gt;Kafka&lt;/strong&gt; or similar high-throughput event-streaming technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive backend production experience with &lt;strong&gt;Go&lt;/strong&gt;—writing idiomatic services with clean design patterns, thorough testing, and robust error handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production-level &lt;strong&gt;React and TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt; skills, with the capability to drive and own user-facing features end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;SQL and PostgreSQL&lt;/strong&gt;—including schema design, query optimization, and data modeling for multi-tenant workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb communication abilities—expert at detailing technical trade-offs to PMs, presenting architecture to leadership, and writing comprehensive design documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High tolerance for &lt;strong&gt;ambiguity&lt;/strong&gt;—adept at making decisions with partial data and iterating quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-Have Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in &lt;strong&gt;identity security, IAM, or security posture management&lt;/strong&gt; - familiarity will be good.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in &lt;strong&gt;cybersecurity products&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
