&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is revolutionising cybersecurity by leveraging AI-native technologies to combat modern cyber threats. Behind every fast-moving go-to-market motion is a platform that makes it possible — and that&#39;s what the &lt;strong&gt;AI GTM Platform team&lt;/strong&gt; builds. We&#39;re the engineering team powering the forward-deployed product teams who sit shoulder-to-shoulder with our customers and internal stakeholders, turning enterprise pain points into shipped product on timelines traditional enterprise cycles can&#39;t match.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you love building leverage — tools, systems, and platforms that multiply the impact of others — and want to own products through every stage of their lifecycle, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do as a Software Engineer II&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the AI GTM Platform team, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the platform that powers the field.&lt;/strong&gt; Design and ship the internal products, APIs, and services that let our forward-deployed teams prototype, validate, and scale customer-facing solutions with unusual speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the full product lifecycle — 0→1, 1→10, and 10→100.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll work across Experimental, Early Access, and General Availability stages of platform products. It&#39;s rare to get to take an idea from a napkin sketch through enterprise-grade rollout; here, you&#39;ll do it, sometimes on multiple products in parallel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work in one of the most dynamic problem spaces in the business.&lt;/strong&gt; GTM is where strategy, customers, product, and revenue converge. Every customer interaction, every deal, every expansion flows through it — and the platforms you build shape how effectively all of that moves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leverage AI-augmented development.&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI coding assistants to enhance productivity, optimise workflows, and automate repetitive work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Combat modern cyber threats at scale.&lt;/strong&gt; Build secure, scalable systems that sit inside a platform processing billions of security events for Fortune 500 enterprises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner closely with customers and the field.&lt;/strong&gt; Work with the people closest to our enterprise customers to understand real problems, iterate quickly, and deliver solutions that compound over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for engineers who have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional experience in software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backend development experience with Python, TypeScript, or Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid fundamentals in at least one modern frontend framework (React, Angular, or Vue). AI accelerates a lot of the implementation work here — what matters is that you can read generated code critically, tell good patterns from bad, and ship frontends you&#39;d be comfortable defending in review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with — or genuine curiosity and willingness to learn — AI coding assistants as part of your everyday workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience or strong interest in building scalable, enterprise-grade applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure) and containerization (Docker, Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong fundamentals in computer science, data structures, and performance optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal platforms, developer tools, or systems used by other engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in taking products through multiple maturity stages (prototype → pilot → scale).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to GTM, sales engineering, solutions engineering, or other customer-facing engineering environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Abnormal Security — and Why This Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A rare breadth of surface area.&lt;/strong&gt; Most platform roles specialise in one stage of maturity. Here, you&#39;ll operate across experimental prototypes, early-access pilots with design partners, and fully productised GA systems — and learn how each stage demands a different kind of engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build for the sharpest users you&#39;ll ever have.&lt;/strong&gt; Your internal users are the technical, fast-moving teams closest to our enterprise customers. They&#39;ll give you direct, high-signal feedback and put what you ship into customers&#39; hands quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct line to business impact.&lt;/strong&gt; GTM platforms are measured by how much faster the business moves as a result. Your work compounds across every customer engagement, every quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-native engineering culture.&lt;/strong&gt; We expect AI-assisted development — it&#39;s how we stay small, fast, and ambitious. You&#39;ll have real room to experiment with and shape how the team uses these tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission that matters.&lt;/strong&gt; The systems you build ultimately protect the world&#39;s largest enterprises from sophisticated cyber attacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready to be part of the AI transformation at Abnormal Security?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
